course: dictionary
lesson: 5063
title: Inspection: a careful check
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An inspection is a careful look at something to check that it is right, safe or in good condition. Inspectors look closely and check every part. Context gives you the clues: «In the UK every zoo needs a licence and regular inspections, and some zoos have been closed after failing them.» Regular checks, a licence and closing after failing all point to a check that a zoo must pass.
explain: The word also means an official visit to check a place. «"Requires improvement" is an official UK inspection grade» is a grade given after an official visit to a school. Here inspection means the official check itself, not just a quick look.
explain: Try the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence: «every zoo needs regular careful checks». It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: An inspection is a careful look to check that something is right, safe or in good condition.
fact: An inspection can also be an official visit to check a place, such as a school, a restaurant or a car.
fact: «Inspection» is a noun. Its plural is inspections.
fact: Useful phrases: on closer inspection, carry out an inspection, safety inspection and inspection day.
fact: On closer inspection means after looking more carefully at something.
exercise: «Every zoo needs regular inspections.» What is an inspection? | *A careful check to see that something is safe and right | A ticket to get into the zoo | A loud noise made by the zoo animals | A kind of animal that lives in the zoo
exercise: A school receives the grade «requires improvement» after its inspection. What did the inspection do? | *Officially checked the school | Closed the school for the summer | Painted the classrooms | Gave the school a new playground
exercise: A sergeant holds a uniform inspection. What is he doing? | Hiding the uniforms in a cupboard | *Looking carefully to check that each uniform is right | Cooking lunch for the soldiers | Telling jokes to the soldiers
test: Which phrase means after looking more carefully? | *On closer inspection | Carry out an inspection | Inspection day | Safety inspection
test: Which sentence uses inspection to mean an official visit? | The car needed a new tyre. | The children played a game in the park. | Snow fell all afternoon. | *The inspectors visited the school to check it.
exam: Some zoos have been closed after failing their inspections. What does failing an inspection most likely mean? | Being too popular with visitors | *Not passing the official check | Winning a competition for animals | Being given a prize for the best zoo
